README.md:25:Project search / Search projects and Task search / Search tasks apply substring queries with ASCII-only case folding. Surrounding whitespace is trimmed; internal whitespace and non-ASCII case remain significant. Blank queries match everything. Project search intersects Active/Archived, and task search intersects completion, priority, and the applied due range. Draft queries take effect only on search submission. Applied queries survive filter changes and edits, including creation and movement, without changing saved data or all-task summaries. Search stays usable when archived. Navigation to the project list (including Projects) or opening a project resets its page-local search to empty.
README.md:33:Tests start real server processes with a temporary SQLite database and verify health, input validation, creation order, project lookup, task ownership, completion updates, page/asset routes, archive/restore, project and task renaming and archived rename protection, completion summaries, independent task priorities and their validation/archive protection, project default inheritance and independence, legacy database migration, and persistence after process restarts. Date tests additionally cover leap-year and format boundaries, clearing, independent task dates, migration, rename preservation, archived protection, filter retention, failure recovery, and restart persistence. Temporary files are removed afterward. Dependency-free browser-entry-point tests additionally exercise all combined filter values, selection retention, task-edit re-filtering, renamed checkbox labels, default-setting saves and failure recovery, and archived filtering/edit controls using a minimal DOM adapter. Range tests cover inclusive and one-sided boundaries, undated tasks, all filter intersections, invalid-range recovery, draft/applied separation, edit-driven membership changes, archived controls, and reopening defaults. Move tests cover destination options, disabled controls, filter and range retention, failure recovery, server validation, archived sources/destinations, append order independent of IDs, new-task order after moves, completion summaries, blank and saved dates, repeated moves, and restart persistence. Return-order tests cover reverse returns, reserved slots in empty projects, independent histories across three projects, current-field preservation, archive/restore, renaming, and migration from existing non-ID task order. Search tests cover ASCII case folding, significant internal whitespace and non-ASCII case, applied/draft separation, all filter intersections, edit-driven membership, creation and movement, summaries, archived controls, and navigation resets.
